 "capsule": "From the permanent union of Castile and León under Ferdinand III in 1230, the Crown of Castile (Corona de Castilla) became the dominant power of the Reconquista, taking Córdoba in 1236 and Seville in 1248. Its 1469 dynastic marriage of Isabella I and Ferdinand II of Aragon created the joint rule of the \"Catholic Monarchs,\" who completed the conquest of Granada in 1492 and sponsored Columbus's first voyage, and the crown passed to their grandson Charles I in 1516, laying the institutional basis for a unified Spanish monarchy.",
